mcp-servers-for-revit, Revara fork (branches revara and revara-installer)

This fork is based on mcp-servers-for-revit (https://github.com/mcp-servers-for-revit/mcp-servers-for-revit),
main at 86cf705, under the MIT License in LICENSE.

Changes in this fork, in the plugin's socket layer and, on branch revara-installer, in the build configuration:
- plugin/Core/MessageFramer.cs is taken unchanged from mcp-servers-for-revit pull request #60 by
  Omar-Elwazeery (commit a4ada37, https://github.com/mcp-servers-for-revit/mcp-servers-for-revit/pull/60),
  MIT License. It joins socket reads into whole JSON messages, so requests longer than 8192 bytes work.
- plugin/Core/SocketService.cs, also from that pull request: uses the framer, listens on loopback only,
  closes a connection that sends something that is not JSON, writes one response per line, and reports a
  listener that fails to start (for example, the port taken by another Revit) instead of claiming success.
  On branch revara, the session token of that pull request is not included; on branch revara-installer it is (see below).
- plugin/Properties/AssemblyInfo.cs: file version 1.0.0.1, informational version 1.0.0-revara.1.
- Revit 2027 (Release R27, net10) configurations and a CI matrix for Revit 2025, 2026 and 2027, on branch revara-installer; file version 1.0.0.2, informational version 1.0.0-revara.2.
- plugin/Core/ConnectionInfoFile.cs and the session token (SessionToken.cs, the auth check in BridgeProtocol.cs)
  are adapted from that pull request (commit a4ada37): the plugin writes its port and a per-session token to
  %LOCALAPPDATA%\Revara\connection.json and rejects requests without that token. The file is written atomically,
  and only after the listener has bound.
- Revara identity on branch revara-installer: its own add-in file (revara-mcp.addin), ClientId, VendorId,
  folder (revara_mcp), ribbon panel (Revara MCP) and ports (38080 to 38089). The assembly names stay
  RevitMCPPlugin and RevitMCPCommandSet. The upstream server in server/ still connects to port 8080 without a
  token, so it does not work with this plugin.
- get_version and health methods, error responses that carry the request id, and an autoStart setting in %LOCALAPPDATA%\Revara\plugin-settings.json (off when that file says false or cannot be read);
  file version 1.0.0.3, informational version 1.0.0-revara.3.
- commandset/Utils/GeometryUtils.cs: on Revit 2027, FindIntersection uses Curve.Intersect(Curve,
  CurveIntersectResultOption.Detailed), because the overload with an out parameter no longer exists there.

No command was added or changed. The socket layer answers two methods of its own, get_version and health. On branch revara, only Revit 2025 (Release R25) is built and tested. On branch revara-installer, Revit 2025 and 2026 (net8) and Revit 2027 (net10) are built in CI and not yet tested in Revit.
